# AI contribution note: Codex wrote all requests in this file.
# [AI: Codex] BEGIN task API test cases
# Run in order against a freshly started app. Users 1 and 2 must exist.
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8000

### 1. GET all tasks — expected: 200 with tasks array
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Accept: application/json

### 2. GET a single task — expected: 200 with task object
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/1
Accept: application/json

### 3. GET a nonexistent task — expected: 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/tasks/999999

### 4. POST a new task — expected: 201 with created task
# @name createTask
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Assignment 1",
  "description": "Extend the REST API with tasks",
  "user_id": 1,
  "completed": false
}

### 5. POST with missing title — expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "description": "Missing title",
  "user_id": 1
}

### 6. POST with nonexistent user_id — expected: 400
POST {{baseUrl}}/tasks
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Invalid owner",
  "user_id": 999999
}

### 7. PUT update the task from case 4 — expected: 200 with updated task
PUT {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Complete Assignment 1 Updated",
  "completed": true
}

### 8. DELETE the task from case 4 — expected: 204
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/tasks/{{createTask.response.body.$.id}}

### 9. GET tasks for user 1 — expected: 200 with only user 1's tasks
GET {{baseUrl}}/users/1/tasks
Accept: application/json

# [AI: Codex] END task API test cases
